WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:03.296
Selective laser trabeculoplasty explained.

2
00:00:03.746 --> 00:00:09.017
Who benefits from first-line laser, what to expect after treatment and how long the effect lasts.

3
00:00:09.467 --> 00:00:12.718
Up to half of patients do not use drops as prescribed.

4
00:00:13.168 --> 00:00:18.172
Simple regimens, instillation training and regular review of technique improve outcomes.

5
00:00:18.622 --> 00:00:21.640
Review frequency depends on stage and stability.

6
00:00:22.090 --> 00:00:26.258
Progression on fields or imaging should prompt a change in the target or the treatment.

7
00:00:26.708 --> 00:00:32.560
Age, family history, high myopia and raised intraocular pressure are the strongest risk factors.

8
00:00:33.010 --> 00:00:39.326
Many patients have no symptoms until visual field loss is advanced, which is why opportunistic checks matter.
